# Secrets for Kazari. Copy to /etc/kazari/kazari.env (systemd; mode 0600)
# or to .env beside compose.yml. Each value is read by the ${NAME} reference
# in kazari.yaml, or applies as a KAZARI_* override; a variable already set
# in the process environment wins over this file. A secret can also come
# from a file, for Docker and Kubernetes secrets, by adding _FILE to its
# name: KAZARI_TLS_DNS_API_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/dns-token.

# The DNS provider's credential, for the wildcard certificate
# (https://kazari.io/docs/certificates/ lists what each provider needs):
KAZARI_TLS_DNS_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: a token for the admin API from other machines. On the server's
# host, kazari admin commands use the socket and need none. At least 32
# characters, for example from: openssl rand -hex 32
# KAZARI_AUTH_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# Once sign-in through an identity provider is configured:
# KAZARI_AUTH_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Docker Compose only: the image tag, which compose.yml reads (default
# latest). Pin a release to upgrade on purpose:
# KAZARI_VERSION=0.3.0
